<section class="prose">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Urban Exposed is a record of the places time forgot — hospitals,
    factories, homes, and everything in between, explored and photographed
    before they're gone for good.
  </p>
  <p>
    I keep exact locations vague on purpose. These places are often
    structurally unsafe, sometimes legally off-limits, and easily damaged by
    vandalism or overcrowding once word gets out. Sharing the photos and the
    stories without the pin drop is how I keep exploring them, and how they
    stay standing a little longer.
  </p>
  <p>
    The one exception: once a place has actually been demolished, there's
    nothing left to protect — so those locations get shared.
  </p>
  <p>
    Thanks for looking.
  </p>
</section>
